{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Q99ipCkUcTwvFsnZoX5N7F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty** that runs as a persistent local web app: `anchor_gui.py` is a stdlib-only Python HTTP server (the `anchor` NSSM Windows service) binding `http://localhost:8777`, which generates the full dashboard on every request and reads/writes plain markdown files directly.\n\n- **Markdown files are the source of truth** â€” no database. `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files (`domains/academic.md`, `commercial.md`, `family.md`, `writing.md`), plus archive files (`CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`). Everything lives in one folder, `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” no OneDrive, no syncing, version-controlled via local Git.\n\n- **Core task management:** capture/add tasks and ideas, move them through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored), with priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields. Fully interactive in the browser; also driveable via the `anchor.py` CLI mirror, which additionally generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown a large \"R&D control surface\"** layered on top of the task system â€” a per-project cockpit for running the **trio of agent skills** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, isolated sessions. This has been built across four versioned waves (v2 sessions/summaries/grass; v3 \"Mission Control\"; v4 \"Project Cockpit,\" merged to master 2026-06-13).\n\n- **What the R&D surface ships:** real ConPTY interactive terminals (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, cached + grounded auto-summaries, per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass-idea board, type-aware deliverable launch, an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **Reliability is built in:** a daily 5:00 AM health-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway test server, exercises every endpoint and the full v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (all model calls stubbed, never live `claude`), and writes a dated report â€” surfacing a red dashboard banner on failure.\n\n- **Deliberate constraints:** Python stdlib only, with **one declared exception** â€” the optional `pywinpty` for the v3 terminal subsystem (lazy import in `pty_manager.py` only; degrades gracefully if absent). `distro.py` enforces no other native/third-party imports. Must run on any machine with Python 3.8+."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eb1a956-0dc9-4f88-9860-f833708fea97","uuid":"eaef1226-63f5-471e-8d98-7d804304e682","request_id":"req_011Cc2Mn6NFipXXsMZxQqD6U"}
